{"packet":0,"rowIndex":363,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":371,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,372]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:371:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D52"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/50/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/50/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=1]Two ideas that contrast each other, they vibrate against each other and change the context of each other.","sourceSha256":"c7c528745bfe9235f43a372d1cf4b3f9b24858573ca133a7942b0ad654d0c3f0"}}
{"packet":0,"rowIndex":364,"value":{"context":{"actorId":"14","conditions":"","conversantId":"1","conversation":"dates/oliverCoyotes/dialogue2","conversationId":303,"entryId":372,"field":"Dialogue Text","next":[[303,373]],"script":""},"family":"dialogue","id":"ds:303:372:Dialogue Text","preserveExactly":false,"selectors":[{"asset":{"$r":"D52"},"kind":"field","pathId":-9011735310751668748,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/51/fields/6/value"},{"asset":"sharedassets0.assets","kind":"field","pathId":3336,"pointer":"/conversations/301/dialogueEntries/51/fields/6/value"}],"source":"[pic=4]The poem is meant to capture both, the phenomena of an instant of observing water, yet the realization that every droplet of water is new.","sourceSha256":"6485f55a9d2250d31fcec3b389223b4ad5040c271c44e0170694033aefd6d97c"}}
